# PSR-4b-http-alias — expire bare `/http` subpath

## Scope

| Work | Done |
| --- | --- |
| Retarget code consumers `…/http` → `…/host/http` | Yes (10 files) |
| Remove `apps/api/tsconfig.json` bare `/http` path aliases | Yes |
| Keep `host/http` tsconfig paths | Yes |
| Rewrite historical audit YAML mentions | **No** (frozen snapshots) |
| Absorb product-named configure adapters | **No** (PSR-4b-configure-2) |

Land commit: `7ffa0774`

Closes deferred item `PSR-4b-configure-http-alias-expiry` from
[`psr-4b-configure-inventory.yaml`](./psr-4b-configure-inventory.yaml).

## Why

Encapsulation SoT already maps:

| Former | Canonical |
| --- | --- |
| `@app-tour/workspace-denali/http` | `…/host/http` |
| `@app-tour/workspace-urban/http` | `…/host/http` |

Configure adapters were retargeted in PSR-4b-configure; tests and one guard
string still used the bare alias via tsconfig. This wave removes that escape
hatch so package `exports` (`./host/http`) are the only resolution path.

## Retargeted

Nine API specs/tests + `scripts/guards/phase-10-guard.mjs` messaging.

## Ratchet

```bash
node scripts/ops/psr-4b-http-alias-smoke.mjs
```

| Check | Ceiling |
| --- | ---: |
| bare `/http` under `apps|packages|scripts` | **0** |
| tsconfig bare `/http` paths | **0** |
| tsconfig `host/http` paths present | required |

## Explicit non-goals

- Deleting denali/urban `http/configure-*` product adapters
- Editing frozen PSR-4b neutrality inventory rows that record old import strings
